# API Route Conventions — AwaazOS

## Route template

```ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { z } from "zod";
import { prisma } from "@/lib/prisma";
import { requireVendorRole, AuthError, PlanGateError } from "@/lib/rbac";

export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";
export const runtime = "nodejs";

const bodySchema = z.object({ /* ... */ });

export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
  try {
    const { vendor, setVendorCookie } = await requireVendorRole("CASHIER", undefined, req);
    const body = bodySchema.parse(await req.json());

    const result = await prisma.entity.create({
      data: { ...body, vendorId: vendor.id },
    });

    const res = NextResponse.json({ data: result }, { status: 201 });
    if (setVendorCookie) {
      res.cookies.set("awz_vendor", setVendorCookie, {
        path: "/", httpOnly: true, sameSite: "lax", secure: process.env.NODE_ENV === "production",
      });
    }
    return res;
  } catch (err) {
    // PlanGateError extends AuthError — catch it first or the body loses its fields.
    if (err instanceof PlanGateError) {
      return NextResponse.json(
        {
          error: err.message,
          code: "plan_upgrade_required",
          requiredPlan: err.required,
          currentPlan: err.current,
          feature: "<feature_key>",
        },
        { status: err.status },
      );
    }
    if (err instanceof AuthError) {
      return NextResponse.json({ error: err.message }, { status: err.status });
    }
    if (err instanceof z.ZodError) {
      return NextResponse.json({ error: "Invalid input", issues: err.issues }, { status: 400 });
    }
    console.error("[api]", err);
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "Internal server error" }, { status: 500 });
  }
}
```

## Response shapes (consistent across the app)

| Method | Success | Status |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` (list) | `{ data: T[] }` (exception: `GET /api/transactions` returns `{ items, page, limit, total, hasMore }`) | 200 |
| `GET` (single) | `{ data: T }` or `{ error: "Not found" }` | 200 / 404 |
| `POST` (create) | `{ data: T }` | 201 |
| `PATCH` / `PUT` | `{ data: T }` | 200 |
| `DELETE` | `{ success: true }` | 200 |
| Validation fail | `{ error: string, issues?: ZodIssue[] }` | 400 |
| Auth fail | `{ error: string }` | 401 / 403 |
| Plan gate | `{ error: "Plan upgrade required", code: "plan_upgrade_required", requiredPlan, currentPlan, feature }` | 402 |
| Not found | `{ error: "Not found" }` | 404 (don't leak existence cross-tenant) |
| Server error | `{ error: "Internal server error" }` | 500 |

## File placement

- `app/api/<resource>/route.ts` — collection (GET list, POST create)
- `app/api/<resource>/[id]/route.ts` — item (GET, PATCH, DELETE)
- `app/api/<resource>/[id]/<action>/route.ts` — sub-actions
- `app/api/webhooks/<provider>/route.ts` — external webhooks (signature-verified)

## Webhook routes

- Skip `requireVendorRole` (no session). Verify HMAC signature first
  (compare with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`, as `verifyRazorpaySignature()` in
  `lib/razorpay.ts` does).
- Put them under `app/api/webhooks/`. The `middleware.ts` matcher excludes
  `api/webhooks` entirely, so middleware never runs on them. Nothing needs adding
  to `lib/auth.config.ts` (its `authorized` callback already returns `true` for
  every `/api/*` path so handlers can answer with JSON 401/403/402).
- Always return 200 to acknowledge receipt — re-queue work via BullMQ if
  the handler is slow.

## Pagination defaults

- Offset pagination: `?page=<n>&limit=<n>`, page size 20 by default, max 100.
  There is no cursor pagination.
- Parse with `parseTransactionListQuery()` (`lib/transaction-list-params.ts`),
  which also handles the `paymentStatus` / `paymentMethod` / `source` filters
  and IST `from` / `to` day ranges. `hasMore = page * limit < total`.

## Caching

- `export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"` for any vendor-scoped route
  (do NOT cache cross-tenant).
- `export const runtime = "nodejs"` — Prisma not edge-safe.
